    "name": "SF-485 - Functional Currency Mandatory - API Tests",
    "description": "API - SF-485 - Make Functional_Currency__c mandatory for Insurer, Insurer Branch and Reinsurer\n\n══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\nGenerated: 2026-01-18\nUpdated: Fixed SOQL query definitions\n══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\nSUMMARY:\n  Make Functional_Currency__c mandatory for Insurer, Insurer Branch and Reinsurer\n\nDESCRIPTION:\n  As a Product Owner / Data Owner I want the Functional_Currency__c field to be \n  mandatory for Insurer, Insurer Branch and Reinsurer records So that every Insurer, \n  Insurer Branch and Reinsurer record has a defined functional currency for reporting, \n  accounting and downstream processing, and no record of those types can be created \n  or saved without a valid value.\n\nACCOUNT TYPES REQUIRING FUNCTIONAL_CURRENCY__C:\n  - Insurer\n  - Insurer Branch\n  - Reinsurer\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA:\n  1. Functional_Currency__c is mandatory for Insurer, Insurer Branch, and Reinsurer\n  2. Save is blocked if Functional_Currency__c is blank\n  3. Error message: \"Functional Currency is required for this record type.\"\n  4. Enforcement works for UI, API, integrations and automated processes\n\nAPI TESTING REQUIREMENTS:\n  - Verify field exists on Lead and Account\n  - Create Account with Functional_Currency__c (Insurer, Insurer Branch, Reinsurer)\n  - Reject Account creation without Functional_Currency__c for required types\n  - Update operations validation\n  - Query operations with proper SOQL\n  - Negative/boundary scenarios\n\nGenerated from: src/features/api/SF/SF-485.feature\n\nThis collection contains API tests for SF-485 work item.\n\nQUERY FORMAT NOTES:\n  - Single record retrieval: GET /sobjects/{object}/{id}?fields=...\n  - SOQL queries: GET /query?q=SELECT... (URL-encoded)\n  - All queries properly formatted for Postman import",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
